		(property "Substitution basis" "DECISIONS.md D24 requires a series diode between the cell and the device: an NFC field pushes current backwards through parasitic diodes and a CR2032 does not tolerate it. A Schottky is CHOSEN over an ideal-diode controller because this board is a first-article test, and its forward drop is the reason the flash here must work down to 1.65 V."
