				)
				(justify left)
				(hide yes)
			)
		)
		(property "Substitution basis" "Apple's flash is a GD25LQ32C, which O'Flynn read out of the LIVE CHIP over SPI - and it is a 1.65-2.0 V part that CANNOT run on this board's 3 V rail. The MX25R is the same 32 Mbit density, runs 1.65-3.6 V so it works at both ends of the cell's discharge AND behind D1's forward drop, and is the lowest-power SPI NOR in KiCad's library. THIS SUBSTITUTION IS FORCED BY DELETING THE 1.8 V RAIL, and is the clearest example on this sheet of one departure making another necessary."
			(at 396.24 57.15 0)
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1.27 1.27)
				)
				(justify left)
				(hide yes)
			)
		)
