	(text "PWR_FLAG: this rail has no power_out pin anywhere on it, so ERC\ncannot see what drives it. The flag says a source is off-sheet.\nA rail a regulator drives does NOT get one."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 12.7 311.15 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "11c9ae35-28f6-54c6-8924-8806945736e7")
	)
	(text "halo Replica FAB VARIANT. THIS IS NOT THE REPLICA AND NOTHING ON IT MAY BE CITED AS A FINDING ABOUT THE AIRTAG. The fidelity record is schematic.py\nand NETS.md beside this file, where 13 of 52 nets are MEASURED. HERE EVERY NET AND EVERY VALUE IS CHOSEN. This board exists to be ordered and switched\non."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 12.7 318.77 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "5c53f354-f174-5db5-aa48-d71d04bead8c")
	)
	(text "ONE RAIL. The reconstruction has cell -> diode -> buck -> 1.8 V -> load switch -> 1.8 V flash. This board DELETES the buck and the 1.8 V rail and runs\neverything from the cell, because the nRF52832 is 1.7-3.6 V and spans the whole CR2032 curve. It was forced - KiCad has no coin-cell 1.8 V buck\nsymbol, and a real land pattern under an invented pinout is the J1 defect again - and it is also less to go wrong on a first article."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 12.7 326.39 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "c258c214-f7db-5b72-acb6-4dc9dd7755f5")
	)
	(text "THE FLASH CHANGED BECAUSE THE RAIL DID. Apple's GD25LQ32C is a 1.65-2.0 V part and cannot run at 3 V. The MX25R3235F is the same 32 Mbit at 1.65-3.6\nV, so it works at both ends of the cell's life AND behind D1's forward drop. One departure making another necessary, which is why they are listed\ntogether."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 12.7 334.01 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "af1105f8-dffb-5aa5-a3b8-cb871577a59a")
	)
	(text "WHAT IS NOT HERE: U2 Apple's UWB SiP (never sold to anyone, and a DNP part with a land pattern invites somebody to try to buy one), with ANT3 and the\ncoaxial port; the op-amp (its ROLE is this project's reconstruction, not an observation); the part marked 1A8/1950 (unidentified down to its\nfunction). None of them can be bought, placed, or justified on a board."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 12.7 341.63 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "52b413aa-4a49-521f-93c9-6320318cee43")
	)
	(text "THIS BOARD IS NOT THE SIZE OF AN AIRTAG, AND THAT IS A FORK RATHER THAN A COMPROMISE. Dimensional fidelity and buildability are in DIRECT CONFLICT\nhere: Apple's WLCSP-50 fits the ~6 mm annular ring and CANNOT BE LANDED, because no complete ball map for it has ever been published. The QFN-48 is\nthe same die, CAN be landed, and is 6x6 mm - which does not fit that ring. There is no arrangement that is both. THIS IS THE BUILDABLE BRANCH; the\ndimensional branch is the metrology record in pcb/, where the 0.30 mm board and the wafer-scale packages live. A person holding a board that works but\nis the wrong shape should not have to work out why."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 12.7 349.25 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "6523502d-2771-5750-87a7-838ae506241c")
	)
	(text "THE FIVE-REMOVALS RESET IS NOT REPRODUCED. Apple has THREE sprung contacts with BOTH positives sensed. A catalogue CR2032 holder has two terminals, so\nthis board senses one positive. A real loss of function, stated rather than quietly dropped."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 12.7 361.95 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "5607f6ab-e8c9-537a-a052-fa51b397fdce")
	)
	(text "THE MATCHING NETWORK C21/L1/C22 AND THE NFC CAPS C23/C24 ARE PLACEHOLDERS, and they are the likeliest things here to be wrong. A match is a\nMEASUREMENT taken against a VNA on the real copper. Start with L1 = 0R and the shunts unfitted. The NFC values depend on a coil that is not wound yet\n- halo_rev_a's first NFC value was EIGHT TIMES WRONG for exactly this reason."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 12.7 367.03 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "a1a14971-81bc-5923-9fe6-50f3922331b1")
	)
	(text "J3 IS SWD AND IT IS THE REASON THIS BOARD CAN BE TRIED AT ALL. Apple's SWD is on bare pads behind APPROTECT. Ours is a header, unlocked. J1 and J2 are\npads for an off-board sounder coil and NFC coil; neither is a part anybody sells."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 12.7 374.65 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "53c4dcd9-1bd1-5098-9c8b-70123bdc1c43")
	)
	(sheet_instances
		(path "/"
			(page "1")
		)
	)
	(embedded_fonts no)
